# MaCSad stateless LOGOS proof-report policy

The mechanical reader supplies strict JSON shape and type facts. This policy
classifies that report, not a case disposition. Axiom count excludes English
Given premises; checked does not claim assumption freedom or independent replay.

## To proofResultStatus (valid: Bool, byteCount: Int, exitCode: Int, axioms: Int, allVerified: Bool, expected: Seq of Text, names: Seq of Text, verified: Seq of Bool, errorNull: Seq of Bool) -> Text:
    If valid is equal to false:
        Return "rejected".
    If byteCount is less than 1:
        Return "rejected".
    If byteCount is greater than 32768:
        Return "rejected".
    If axioms is less than 0:
        Return "rejected".
    If axioms is greater than 4096:
        Return "rejected".
    Let count be length of expected.
    If count is less than 1:
        Return "rejected".
    If count is greater than 32:
        Return "rejected".
    Let nameCountMatches be length of names is equal to count.
    If nameCountMatches is equal to false:
        Return "rejected".
    Let verdictCountMatches be length of verified is equal to count.
    If verdictCountMatches is equal to false:
        Return "rejected".
    Let errorCountMatches be length of errorNull is equal to count.
    If errorCountMatches is equal to false:
        Return "rejected".
    Let seen be a new Seq of Text.
    Let mutable everyVerified be true.
    Let mutable index be 1.
    While index is at most count:
        Let name be item index of expected.
        Let size be length of text_bytes(name).
        If size is less than 1:
            Return "rejected".
        If size is greater than 256:
            Return "rejected".
        Let targetMatches be item index of names is equal to name.
        If targetMatches is equal to false:
            Return "rejected".
        Repeat for previous in seen:
            If previous is equal to name:
                Return "rejected".
        Push name to seen.
        If item index of verified is equal to true:
            If item index of errorNull is equal to false:
                Return "rejected".
        Otherwise:
            Set everyVerified to false.
        Set index to index + 1.
    Let summaryMatches be allVerified is equal to everyVerified.
    If summaryMatches is equal to false:
        Return "rejected".
    If everyVerified:
        If exitCode is equal to 0:
            Return "checked".
    Otherwise:
        If exitCode is equal to 1:
            Return "not-proved".
    Return "rejected".

## Test: Proof result reports checked under supplied assumptions
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, true, ["Socrates"], ["Socrates"], [true], [true]) is equal to "checked".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 200, 0, 2, true, ["A", "B"], ["A", "B"], [true, true], [true, true]) is equal to "checked".
## Test: Proof result retains not proved
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 1, 1, false, ["A"], ["A"], [false], [false]) is equal to "not-proved".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 1, 0, false, ["A"], ["A"], [false], [true]) is equal to "not-proved".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 200, 1, 2, false, ["A", "B"], ["A", "B"], [true, false], [true, false]) is equal to "not-proved".
## Test: Proof result rejects malformed transport
    For all booleans allVerified:
        Expect that proofResultStatus(false, 120, 0, 0, allVerified, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
## Test: Proof result requires exact unique targets
    Let absent be a new Seq of Text.
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, true, absent, absent, [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, true, [""], [""], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, true, ["A"], ["B"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 200, 0, 0, true, ["A", "A"], ["A", "A"], [true, true], [true, true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 200, 0, 0, true, ["A", "B"], ["B", "A"], [true, true], [true, true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true, true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true, true]) is equal to "rejected".
## Test: Proof result rejects inconsistent checker fields
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [false]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 1, 0, true, ["A"], ["A"], [false], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 1, 0, false, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 1, 0, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 0, false, ["A"], ["A"], [false], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 124, 0, false, ["A"], ["A"], [false], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
## Test: Proof result enforces byte and axiom bounds
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 0, 0, 0, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 32769, 0, 0, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, -1, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 120, 0, 4097, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 32768, 0, 4096, true, ["A"], ["A"], [true], [true]) is equal to "checked".
## Test: Proof result measures target names in UTF8 bytes
    Let accepted be repeatText("é", 128).
    Let excessive be repeatText("é", 129).
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 1024, 0, 0, true, [accepted], [accepted], [true], [true]) is equal to "checked".
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 1024, 0, 0, true, [excessive], [excessive], [true], [true]) is equal to "rejected".
## Test: Proof result caps requested theorem count
    Let names be a new Seq of Text.
    Let flags be a new Seq of Bool.
    Let mutable index be 1.
    While index is at most 32:
        Push numText(index) to names.
        Push true to flags.
        Set index to index + 1.
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 4096, 0, 0, true, names, names, flags, flags) is equal to "checked".
    Push "33" to names.
    Push true to flags.
    Expect that proofResultStatus(true, 4096, 0, 0, true, names, names, flags, flags) is equal to "rejected".
